{"id":161229982,"slug":"transcranial-focused-ultrasound-tfus-578","title":"Transcranial Focused Ultrasound (tFUS) Will Blow Your Mind","subtitle":"It's a remarkable technology in the making","post_date":"2025-06-30T17:59:38.523Z","audience":"everyone","type":"newsletter","canonical_url":"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/transcranial-focused-ultrasound-tfus-578","wordcount":611,"source":"api","fetched_at":"2026-09-13T21:46:59.045Z","body_sha256":"d6fa4859cfedba0aef03305db6107428af7b4e7c579b2656d1cba9adcc9cda75","text_words":709,"complete":true,"body_html":"<p>The Frontier Psychiatrists is a regular-enough health-themed newsletter.  I’ve briefly introduced the world to transcranial focused ultrasound <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/transcranial-focused-ultrasound-tfus?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">in this previous article.</a></p><div class=\"digest-post-embed\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;nodeId&quot;:&quot;cadafb6b-e498-4578-be55-70bc2091851e&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists is on the cutting edge of letting the general public know what the editor of the publication thinks is coming next. My track record is pretty good—I called ERISA lawsuits about health plan PBM nonsense, I called accelerated TMS&quot;,&quot;cta&quot;:&quot;Read full story&quot;,&quot;showBylines&quot;:true,&quot;showDescription&quot;:true,&quot;showImage&quot;:true,&quot;size&quot;:&quot;sm&quot;,&quot;isEditorNode&quot;:true,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;Transcranial Focused Ultrasound (tFUS) is Coming to Brain Health&quot;,&quot;publishedBylines&quot;:[{&quot;id&quot;:2277375,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Owen Scott Muir, M.D, DFAACAP&quot;,&quot;bio&quot;:&quot;Dr. Owen Scott Muir, M.D., DFAACAP is the Chief Medical Officer of Radial &amp; Neurolief. He's a graduate of Amherst College, Child, Adolescent, and Adult Psychiatrist, and a prolific writer and podcaster. https://www.meetradial.com for more.&quot;,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F1c03f44d-4506-4843-989f-0d38e66c6946_400x400.jpeg&quot;,&quot;is_guest&quot;:false,&quot;bestseller_tier&quot;:100}],&quot;post_date&quot;:&quot;2024-09-20T16:28:45.767Z&quot;,&quot;cover_image&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!k9ks!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5ddc9a0c-a97e-48c3-9a3e-1a8fd8fbf8dd_1238x724.heic&quot;,&quot;cover_image_alt&quot;:null,&quot;canonical_url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/transcranial-focused-ultrasound-tfus&quot;,&quot;section_name&quot;:null,&quot;video_upload_id&quot;:null,&quot;id&quot;:149104965,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;newsletter&quot;,&quot;reaction_count&quot;:7,&quot;comment_count&quot;:2,&quot;publication_id&quot;:null,&quot;publication_name&quot;:&quot;The Frontier Psychiatrists &quot;,&quot;publication_logo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!oO3w!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fbucketeer-e05bbc84-baa3-437e-9518-adb32be77984.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F997b8496-9b4d-43c2-b393-6f8a77945b00_1080x1080.png&quot;,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;youtube_url&quot;:null,&quot;show_links&quot;:null,&quot;feed_url&quot;:null}\"></div><p>Ultrasound is a technology that is easy to feel comfortable with. It's the same technology used to measure your baby’s heartbeat, which is some positive association if ever there was one.</p><p>Ultrasound is a really, really high-pitched sound wave.  Audible sounds, traveling through mediums like air, make it vibrate, and make our eardrums vibrate, and that in turn, when trans-coded into neural signals by the cochlea, makes sounds things we can hear.  Those sounds range between 20hz and 20,000 Hz (also written 20 kHz).   Ultrasound begins where human hearing ends, at approximately 20 kHz and above.</p><p>We have used ultrasound to travel through human bodies, bounce back, and use those reflections to capture an image, just like we use radar and sonar.  The wave hits an object and bounces back; we recreate an image from the reflections.</p><p>You can “see” inside the body, without harming it, which is awesome. He’s a neonatal brain, imaged with ultrasound: </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic\" width=\"452\" height=\"410.14814814814815\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:588,&quot;width&quot;:648,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:452,&quot;bytes&quot;:41525,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/161229982?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!yNR7!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F741d0997-0c9e-465a-bc12-e6e7ad086032_648x588.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p> Jay Sanguinetti, Ph.D. has been working with this modality for years.  Just recently, he formerly brought his company, Sanmai, out of “stealth.”</p><p>“Stealth” is a concept that I take some issue with, in that it’s a way for companies that no one has ever heard of to stay that way.  You know, to sneak into the market and change everything!   As a fan of organic growth strategies and earned media, the most stealthy thing about all brain stimulation companies is the same: people think pills exist, and maybe therapy, but want neither, and what are you talking about?  Ultrawhat?  For your brain? </p><p>Exactly.  However, I’m a big fan of obscure sounds—see my prior writing on <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/why-isnt-becks-colors-heralded-as?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">Beck</a>, <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/american-football?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">American Football</a>, and <a href=\"https://open.substack.com/pub/thefrontierpsychiatrists/p/neuromodulation-via-modest-mouse?r=1ct8f&amp;utm_campaign=post&amp;utm_medium=web&amp;showWelcomeOnShare=false\">Modest Mouse</a>!  tFUS is the indie rock band of the treatment of brain disorders without pills or therapy space.</p><p>Jay—along with many others on his team, like the inimitable <span class=\"mention-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Sharena Rice, PhD&quot;,&quot;id&quot;:135623193,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;user&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:null,&quot;photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/f81b72ad-b6cf-4ce3-85d2-dd0503b37e6f_633x633.jpeg&quot;,&quot;uuid&quot;:&quot;f632521f-6d1a-4430-a423-8f92575edcef&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"MentionToDOM\"></span>—are now able to tell you, publicly, what they are up to.</p><div id=\"youtube2-RCep9f-7I_0\" class=\"youtube-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;videoId&quot;:&quot;RCep9f-7I_0&quot;,&quot;startTime&quot;:null,&quot;endTime&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"Youtube2ToDOM\"><div class=\"youtube-inner\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/RCep9f-7I_0?rel=0&amp;autoplay=0&amp;showinfo=0&amp;enablejsapi=0\" frameborder=\"0\" loading=\"lazy\" gesture=\"media\" allow=\"autoplay; fullscreen\" allowautoplay=\"true\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" width=\"728\" height=\"409\"></iframe></div></div><p>It’s not trivial.  It could heal deep regions of the brain that have required surgery in the past, non-invasively.  It could do a lot of things.  However, it exists.  </p><p>As science.  Now!  And you can know that tFUS changes the Brain with non-invasive sound waves, and that is very cool. It can go deep into the brain without surgery.  You can and should be excited. </p><p>It might heal depression, as we see in this graphic from a recent RCT: </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic\" width=\"487\" height=\"418.29147286821706\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:554,&quot;width&quot;:645,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:487,&quot;bytes&quot;:52203,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/heic&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/161229982?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!muWh!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F29e01736-734e-4cae-9628-4fb35c2562c3_645x554.heic 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a><figcaption class=\"image-caption\"><a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11321877/\">The paper is available here.</a></figcaption></figure></div><p>It might heal anxiety:</p><blockquote><p>Wilcoxon Signed-Rank Test comparison of pre- and post-tfUS resulted in a significant decrease in anxiety as measured by the HAM-A (<em>W =</em> −3.69, <em>p</em> &lt; 0.001, <em>pre-post-Δ</em> = −12.64 + 12.51, effect size = 0.931, power = 99% at alpha = 0.05) and the BAI (<em>W</em> = −3.94, <em>p</em> &lt; 0.001, <em>pre-post-Δ</em> = −12.88 + 10.42, effect size = −0.931, power = 99% at alpha = 0.05).</p><p>Sixteen participants (64%) reported a PGI-I score of &gt;2, indicating significant perceived benefit. Fifteen participants (60%) demonstrated a meaningful reduction (&gt;30%) of HAM-A score at completion. Eight participants (32%) achieved remission of GAD symptoms according to a completion HAM-A score &lt;14.<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-1\" href=\"#footnote-1\" target=\"_self\">1</a></p></blockquote><p></p><p></p><p>It might heal PTSD<a class=\"footnote-anchor\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteAnchorToDOM\" id=\"footnote-anchor-2\" href=\"#footnote-2\" target=\"_self\">2</a>:</p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"917\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:917,&quot;width&quot;:1456,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:497346,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/i/161229982?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!2oIM!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb52b6b5a-d6c0-4631-89cc-2ea58376b7ef_1832x1154.png 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>And dozens of other brain disorders besides.</p><p></p><div><hr></div><p>Greetings, if you (or a loved one) are looking for relief from depression, OCD, anxiety, PTSD, Bipolar Disorder, or other conditions, feel free to explore care with <strong>Radial</strong>—it’s the company of which I’m a co-founder, delivering the most advanced mental health care on earth. <em>If you are looking for help, <strong>Radial</strong> offers the most advanced mental health care.</em></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://meetradial.com/?utm_source=frontier-psychiatrist&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=newsletter&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Get Care At Radial&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:&quot;button-wrapper&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary button-wrapper\" href=\"https://meetradial.com/?utm_source=frontier-psychiatrist&amp;utm_medium=newsletter&amp;utm_campaign=newsletter\"><span>Get Care At Radial</span></a></p><div><hr></div><p>Follow this newsletter for more!</p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/transcranial-focused-ultrasound-tfus-578?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Share&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://thefrontierpsychiatrists.substack.com/p/transcranial-focused-ultrasound-tfus-578?utm_source=substack&utm_medium=email&utm_content=share&action=share\"><span>Share</span></a></p><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-1\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-1\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">1</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Mahdavi, K. D., Jordan, S. E., Jordan, K. G., Rindner, E. S., Haroon, J. M., Habelhah, B., ... &amp; Kuhn, T. P. (2023). A pilot study of low-intensity focused ultrasound for treatment-resistant generalized anxiety disorder. <em>Journal of Psychiatric Research</em>, <em>168</em>, 125-132.</p><p></p></div></div><div class=\"footnote\" data-component-name=\"FootnoteToDOM\"><a id=\"footnote-2\" href=\"#footnote-anchor-2\" class=\"footnote-number\" contenteditable=\"false\" target=\"_self\">2</a><div class=\"footnote-content\"><p>Barksdale, B. R., Enten, L., DeMarco, A., Kline, R., Doss, M. K., Nemeroff, C. B., &amp; Fonzo, G. A. (2025). Low-intensity transcranial focused ultrasound amygdala neuromodulation: a double-blind sham-controlled target engagement study and unblinded single-arm clinical trial. <em>Molecular psychiatry</em>, 1-15.</p><p></p></div></div>","text":"The Frontier Psychiatrists is a regular-enough health-themed newsletter. I’ve briefly introduced the world to transcranial focused ultrasound in this previous article.\n\nUltrasound is a technology that is easy to feel comfortable with. It's the same technology used to measure your baby’s heartbeat, which is some positive association if ever there was one.\n\nUltrasound is a really, really high-pitched sound wave. Audible sounds, traveling through mediums like air, make it vibrate, and make our eardrums vibrate, and that in turn, when trans-coded into neural signals by the cochlea, makes sounds things we can hear. Those sounds range between 20hz and 20,000 Hz (also written 20 kHz). Ultrasound begins where human hearing ends, at approximately 20 kHz and above.\n\nWe have used ultrasound to travel through human bodies, bounce back, and use those reflections to capture an image, just like we use radar and sonar. The wave hits an object and bounces back; we recreate an image from the reflections.\n\nYou can “see” inside the body, without harming it, which is awesome. He’s a neonatal brain, imaged with ultrasound:\n\nJay Sanguinetti, Ph.D. has been working with this modality for years. Just recently, he formerly brought his company, Sanmai, out of “stealth.”\n\n“Stealth” is a concept that I take some issue with, in that it’s a way for companies that no one has ever heard of to stay that way. You know, to sneak into the market and change everything! As a fan of organic growth strategies and earned media, the most stealthy thing about all brain stimulation companies is the same: people think pills exist, and maybe therapy, but want neither, and what are you talking about? Ultrawhat? For your brain?\n\nExactly. However, I’m a big fan of obscure sounds—see my prior writing on Beck , American Football , and Modest Mouse ! tFUS is the indie rock band of the treatment of brain disorders without pills or therapy space.\n\nJay—along with many others on his team, like the inimitable —are now able to tell you, publicly, what they are up to.\n\nIt’s not trivial. It could heal deep regions of the brain that have required surgery in the past, non-invasively. It could do a lot of things. However, it exists.\n\nAs science. Now! And you can know that tFUS changes the Brain with non-invasive sound waves, and that is very cool. It can go deep into the brain without surgery. You can and should be excited.\n\nIt might heal depression, as we see in this graphic from a recent RCT:\n\nThe paper is available here.\n\nIt might heal anxiety:\n\nWilcoxon Signed-Rank Test comparison of pre- and post-tfUS resulted in a significant decrease in anxiety as measured by the HAM-A ( W = −3.69, p < 0.001, pre-post-Δ = −12.64 + 12.51, effect size = 0.931, power = 99% at alpha = 0.05) and the BAI ( W = −3.94, p < 0.001, pre-post-Δ = −12.88 + 10.42, effect size = −0.931, power = 99% at alpha = 0.05).\n\nSixteen participants (64%) reported a PGI-I score of >2, indicating significant perceived benefit. Fifteen participants (60%) demonstrated a meaningful reduction (>30%) of HAM-A score at completion. Eight participants (32%) achieved remission of GAD symptoms according to a completion HAM-A score <14. 1\n\nIt might heal PTSD 2 :\n\nAnd dozens of other brain disorders besides.\n\nGreetings, if you (or a loved one) are looking for relief from depression, OCD, anxiety, PTSD, Bipolar Disorder, or other conditions, feel free to explore care with Radial —it’s the company of which I’m a co-founder, delivering the most advanced mental health care on earth. If you are looking for help, Radial offers the most advanced mental health care.\n\nGet Care At Radial\n\nFollow this newsletter for more!\n\nSubscribe now\n\nShare\n\n1 Mahdavi, K. D., Jordan, S. E., Jordan, K. G., Rindner, E. S., Haroon, J. M., Habelhah, B., ... & Kuhn, T. P. (2023). A pilot study of low-intensity focused ultrasound for treatment-resistant generalized anxiety disorder. Journal of Psychiatric Research , 168 , 125-132.\n\n2 Barksdale, B. R., Enten, L., DeMarco, A., Kline, R., Doss, M. K., Nemeroff, C. B., & Fonzo, G. A. (2025). Low-intensity transcranial focused ultrasound amygdala neuromodulation: a double-blind sham-controlled target engagement study and unblinded single-arm clinical trial. Molecular psychiatry , 1-15."}